      Deadman Timber Tiebacks: Anchoring Landscape Retaining Walls
    </h1>
    <p class="text-base text-gray-600 leading-relaxed max-w-3xl mb-6">
      Gravity retaining walls rely primarily on their own self-weight to hold back retained earth. However, a wooden 6x6 timber wall is relatively lightweight compared to concrete masonry units: a 4-foot timber wall weighs less than 40 lbs per square foot of face. To prevent the massive lateral pressure of the retained hill from toppling the wall forward, you must install <strong>perpendicular "deadman" tieback anchors</strong> extending deep into the stable passive earth zone behind the slope.
    </p>

    <!-- Key Metrics Grid -->
